# Copy this file to ".env" (never commit .env).
#
# These two are the ONLY Supabase values that may ever be inside the app:
#   Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
#   SUPABASE_URL      = "Project URL"
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = "anon public" key (or the new "publishable" key)
SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_OR_ANON_KEY

# NEVER put these in this file, in the app, or in Git:
#   service_role / secret key, database password, access token.
# They live only in GitHub repository secrets.

# ---- AI document analysis (optional) ----
# The AI key is NEVER put in the app. Pick ONE way to give it to the server:
#   A) In the app: App manager -> sparkle icon (AI settings) -> paste the key. It is stored in the database
#      and used for everyone. Nobody can read it back.
#   B) GitHub repository secrets (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions), then run the
#      "Deploy backend" workflow:  AI_API_KEY, optionally AI_PROVIDER (gemini|anthropic) and AI_MODEL.
# With neither, the app falls back to its on-device analysis.
# AI_API_KEY=YOUR_AI_PROVIDER_KEY_HERE
# AI_PROVIDER=gemini
# AI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
